# Frontend Integration Rule

`frontend/` is the **official frontend** and the **source of truth for the presentation layer**. Map only `backend/` ↔ `frontend/`.

Companion rules: `architecture.mdc`, `frontend.mdc`, `ui.mdc`, `api.mdc`.  
Docs: `docs/architecture/frontend-integration.md`, `docs/architecture/frontend-backend-mapping.md`.

## Do

- Preserve the UI library, design system, routing, layouts, navigation, and UX once established.
- Reuse existing components over new ones.
- Prefer updating Go APIs, DTOs, and mappers when the UI expects a different shape.
- Implement missing behavior in the Golang backend before redesigning pages.
- Wire data with thin hooks and adapters.
- Keep image loading on the API stream route (same origin).

## Do not

- Replace the UI kit or redesign screens to fit backend enums.
- Broadly rewrite pages when a backend or adapter change would suffice.
- Introduce a second frontend application for the same inventory product.

## When frontend changes are allowed

Only if the feature cannot be supported from the backend (or the assessment explicitly requires UI). Then: smallest diff, same design language, update docs/mapping if the page contract changes.
